  "delta": {
    "old_hash_v1": 2048,
    "new_real_v1": 16384,
    "mechanism": "Block size is not embedding-geometry sensitive (it turns on column sizes and row counts, not cluster structure) \u2014 but it IS dimension-sensitive. At dim 64 the directory budget admitted 2 KiB blocks; at dim 768 the exact-rerank column is 12x wider, so the same-size directory now costs 12x the bytes per row and blocks below 16 KiB exceed the 4-byte/row openability budget. Among the eligible sizes 16 KiB reads the fewest bytes (391 MB vs 65 KiB's 602 MB \u2014 bigger blocks over-read). Classified geometry-STABLE: re-derive on the COLUMN LAYOUT changing, not per corpus/generation."
  },
  "rule": "minimise physically-read bytes across the golden query set (whole blocks, frame headers, over-read included), SUBJECT TO the block directory staying under 4 bytes/row (the openability policy bound). Ties to the smaller block.",
  "note": "geometry-STABLE, dimension-sensitive. Re-derive with a real-v1 block-size sweep when the column layout (dim, encodings) changes. Every part records its own block size, so a store built at one size is readable whatever this default becomes."
